{
  "method": "Independent physical-covariance and matrix-Taylor audit.\n\nNo trajectories, Monte Carlo sampling, imported manuscript benchmark functions,\nsecular root fitting, or target B4/C6 coefficients enter the computed branch.\n\nRoute A builds the full planar Ito covariance generator in real space, projects\nits symmetric O(2)-scalar covariance sector onto a translation character, and\nonly then checks the manuscript's Fourier equations and secular residual.\n\nRoute B builds a relative-coordinate Bloch matrix from left/right real-space\nstiffness actions and the local momentum-diagonal Ito injection. Its eigenvalue\nTaylor coefficients are obtained by a bordered linear-system recurrence.\nThe closed coefficients are evaluated only afterwards for comparison.\n",
  "inputs_to_independent_computation": [
    "physical Ito drift and site rotation matrices",
    "periodic nearest-neighbor stiffness",
    "uniform O(2)-scalar covariance embedding",
    "relative-coordinate Bloch interpolation",
    "bordered eigenvalue-Taylor recurrence"
  ],
  "not_inputs": [
    "the target quartic/sixth-order coefficients",
    "the manuscript secular equation for root computation",
    "fitted pole values or trajectory samples"
  ],
